      "proposed_at": "2026-11-17T00:00:00Z",
      "motivation": "First proposal of the canonical 0-9 skeleton. The existing plan predates the skeleton (no entry has a section) and is approved, so its 80 entries are untouched except for the narrative_stale flag and the new children of Home; moves and section assignments are proposals only. New content added: reading guide (0), context (1), architecture overview and chapters for the five domains missing from the plan (contacts, process-organizer-core, attachments, special-projects-initiatives, super-admin) (3), six functional areas (4), deliverable cards for interfaces (5) and runbooks (6), traceability (7), open points and documentation gaps (8), and reference groups with 85 pages for nodes not yet in the plan (9). Section 2 is omitted: no approved project plan exists, hence no generated plan pages. Chapter order, with no approved plan, goes from cross-cutting foundations to dependents following relates_to and the discovery context: security, auth, contacts, volunteer-management, process-organizer-core, attachments, device-requests, shipments, special-projects-initiatives (which depends on the checklist and attachment modules), super-admin (platform operations built on the security gate). Section 5 contains only deliverable cards because no formal interface source exists. The plan status is set to draft because the structure changed. Existing Italian titles are not renamed here: titles of protected pages are kept and the language alignment is left to the operator, with their narratives flagged stale.",
